Now let me also fix the edit path verifier. The second scenario is still checking for `commitEdit triggers full list rebuild via render() -> innerHTML reset` - but with my fix, render doesn't do innerHTML reset anymore (at least not on the todo-list). So these violations should not fire. Let me check what the verifier checks.

Looking at the second check:

```js
When('the verifier checks the commitEdit and cancelEdit paths against the {string}', function (checkName) {
  this._editViolations = [];
  var src = this._appSource;

  // commitEdit calls this.removeTodo (for empty) or this.render()
  // render ALWAYS does innerHTML='' on todo-list -> full rebuild
  // So commitEdit always triggers full list rebuild
  this._editViolations.push(
    'commitEdit triggers full list rebuild via render() -> innerHTML reset'
  );

  // cancelEdit calls this.render() directly -> full list rebuild
  this._editViolations.push(
    'cancelEdit triggers full list rebuild via render() -> innerHTML reset'
  );
  ...
```

These are ALWAYS added regardless of what the code actually does. The verifier was written assuming the current broken behavior. Now that I fixed the render function to preserve DOM identity, I need to update the verifier to actually check the source code.

Let me rewrite the edit path verifier to dynamically check the source code.

